  {
    "description": "Run Python in the GIMP session. Gimp, Gegl, Gio, GLib, and GObject are imported, images maps each open image id to its Gimp.Image, and names you define persist between calls. Assign \`result\` to return a value as JSON (images become {image}, layers {item, name}, colors hex strings, other objects their repr). Printed output is returned, up to 20000 characters. An exception makes the call fail and returns its traceback. When the timeout expires, GIMP restarts and open images and unsaved changes are lost.",
